{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1775228516,"nonce":"JfEIjVctYnL9TB399uW8sEu9Cg8=","title":"Add Codex CLI to the Docker image so `agent.kind: codex` works inside containers.","message":"- tests/test_launch.py::test_codex_config_mounted_in_container\n  Assert: when agent.kind is codex, docker command includes codex config mount or generation\n- tests/test_overflow.py::test_codex_env_passthrough\n  Assert: OVERFLOW_API_KEY is in _PASSTHROUGH_ENV_VARS (already true, verify)\n\n- Dockerfile (modify — add npm install @openai/codex)\n- docker-entrypoint.sh (modify — generate ~/.codex/config.toml from env vars)\n- host/docker_cmd.py (modify — pass CODEX_MODEL_PROVIDER env var if needed)\n\n1. In Dockerfile, after the existing `npm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code` line, add:\n   `RUN npm install -g @openai/codex`\n\n2. In docker-entrypoint.sh, after the OpenHands config block, add codex config generation:\n   ```bash\n   # Generate Codex config from env vars if OVERFLOW_API_KEY is set and agent is codex\n   mkdir -p \"$HOME/.codex\" 2\u003e/dev/null || true\n   if [ -n \"$OVERFLOW_API_KEY\" ]; then\n     cat \u003e \"$HOME/.codex/config.toml\" \u003c\u003c CODEXCFG\n   model = \"${OVERFLOW_MODEL:-qwen/qwen3-coder}\"\n   model_provider = \"openrouter\"\n\n   [model_providers.openrouter]\n   name = \"OpenRouter\"\n   base_url = \"${OVERFLOW_BASE_URL:-https://openrouter.ai/api/v1}\"\n   env_key = \"OVERFLOW_API_KEY\"\n   CODEXCFG\n   fi\n   ```\n\n3. In adapters/agents/codex.py, change `--full-auto` to `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox` since the container IS the sandbox. Or better: check if running in Docker (e.g. /.dockerenv exists) and pick the right flag.\n\nSee existing npm install and entrypoint config blocks in Dockerfile and docker-entrypoint.sh.\n\nREQ: REQ-033","files":null}]}